The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
xcc_info = kzalloc(sizeof(struct amdgpu_acpi_xcc_info), GFP_KERNEL);
if (ret == -ENOMEM)
    return ret;
```
Reason: The kzalloc allocates memory for xcc_info. When amdgpu_acpi_dev_init() returns -ENOMEM, the function returns immediately without freeing xcc_info, causing a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (ret == -ENOMEM) {
    kfree(xcc_info);
    return ret;
}
```
Reason: By adding kfree(xcc_info) before returning, the allocated memory is properly freed, preventing the memory leak.

